1. facebook/akd
   Copyright (c) Meta Platforms, Inc. and affiliates.
   Licensed by its authors under MIT OR Apache-2.0. This repository exercises
   the MIT option. Source: https://github.com/facebook/akd

   Aegon began as a fork of the `akd` and `akd_core` crates. The AKD
   directory, its SEEMless/Merkle append-only-tree backend, its storage and
   configuration layers, its wire types, and its API have since been removed.

   What remains from upstream:

     * The ECVRF implementation (ECVRF-EDWARDS25519-SHA512-TAI, RFC 9381) in
       `aegon_crypto::ecvrf`, which the AKD authors adapted from Diem's
       NextGen Crypto module. Modifications made by The Aegon Authors: AKD's
       `VRFKeyStorage` trait and its test key store were removed, and the
       `no_std` import shims were dropped.
     * The `xtask` code-coverage helper.

   Those files carry Meta's copyright header, as MIT requires.

